                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "14816bda-7e41-423b-a29c-0c1cbfd3f0a5",
                        "entry_id": "8133c0d8-00d1-31d9-8ceb-d00d4d85bfba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "couroucous"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1018bac2-e4e5-38cc-b29b-64d57bbf30b3",
                        "entry_id": "8133c0d8-00d1-31d9-8ceb-d00d4d85bfba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce de trogon à couronne bleu métallique, à la tête et la poitrine noire, au dos vert iridescent et au ventre rouge vermillon chez le mâle, dont la queue est légèrement trapéziforme et finement zébrée, répandu dans les forêts tropicales et subtropicales de l'Amérique du Sud (Trogon curucui)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "370a80c7-6245-3daa-a4e7-4b028677d810",
                        "entry_id": "8133c0d8-00d1-31d9-8ceb-d00d4d85bfba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom générique sous lequel on désignait toutes les espèces de trogonidés jusqu'à la fin du XIXᵉ siècle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "666cbf1f-2314-4c5d-89a5-1b9d74498a74",
                                "sense_id": "370a80c7-6245-3daa-a4e7-4b028677d810",
                                "text": "L'ancien nom du quetzal resplendissant était, jusqu'au début du XXe siècle, le couroucou royal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2dc3c47-0ab4-444d-a7a4-e962038a2913",
                                "sense_id": "370a80c7-6245-3daa-a4e7-4b028677d810",
                                "text": "Il se trouve, entre le couroucou à ventre rouge et le couroucou à ventre jaune, quelques variétés que nos nomenclateurs ont prises pour des espèces différentes : par exemple, celui que l'on a décrit sous la dénomination de couroucou de la Guiane n'est qu'une variété d'âge du couroucou à ventre jaune, duquel il ne diffère que par la couleur du dessus du dos, qui dans l'oiseau adulte est d'un beau bleu d'azur, et dans l'oiseau jaune d'une couleur cendrée."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "391ab72d-0a2d-4aa3-9019-3dbcde578a08",
                        "source_entry_id": "8133c0d8-00d1-31d9-8ceb-d00d4d85bfba",
                        "source_sense_description": "Nom désuet des trogonidés",
                        "target_lang_word": "trogon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trogon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3b015f6-f8b3-3ef3-9270-578d35a029a3",
                                        "entry_id": "c1da690e-922f-32a9-a764-e0ecabc6dcab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bird in the family Trogonidae from the order Trogoniformes, most of which live in Central and South America, have colorful feathers, and nest in holes in trees."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00319b6d-bf6f-4682-a89c-81fade7ae4d7",
                        "source_entry_id": "8133c0d8-00d1-31d9-8ceb-d00d4d85bfba",
                        "source_sense_description": "Nom désuet des trogonidés",
                        "target_lang_word": "quetzal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quetzal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                        "entry_id": "454ea17c-26aa-3d82-ab46-a6b20b839381",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any trogon of the genus Pharomacrus, especially a resplendent quetzal (Pharomacrus mocinno), which has very long tail feathers and is found in Guatemala and Costa Rica."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05506556-f638-4129-a04f-834067f2a638",
                                                "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                                "text": "Included among the images that Rigoberta Menchú uses in order to subtly convey her people's ethnicity is an image of Guatemala as the \"land of the quetzal.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcddbdfb-ed8a-4996-b210-d554e3b38833",
                                                "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                                "text": "A strikingly beautiful bird, the quetzal is the national emblem of Guatemala, appearing on its currency and postage. The quetzal ranges from southern Mexico to Costa Rica."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0271f589-8e24-4e64-8334-506a8d158e2d",
                                                "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                                "text": "This particular wild avocado species had beautiful small black fruits set in a red cap that made it easy for the quetzals to find them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                        "entry_id": "454ea17c-26aa-3d82-ab46-a6b20b839381",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A monetary unit used in Guatemala, equal to 100 centavos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81b14f8c-8cb7-4ac9-a51f-c5700cc4925a",
                                                "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                                "text": "In 2002 Guatemala officially declared the U.S. dollar as legal tender to circulate in parallel to the national currency, the quetzal. This is not likely to last for long as the quetzal is not widely accepted and is considered a weak store of value."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abe4daf0-d115-403c-924f-6d9532ee8a21",
                                                "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                                "text": "In this situation, they chose a policy mix of moderate monetary tightening, tight fiscal policy, and central bank intervention in the foreign exchange market to prevent excessive appreciation of the quetzal, without pursuing an exchange rate target[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff688be3-2248-4ac2-bf73-e759e17f3c9f",
                                                "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                                "text": "To cope with the subsequent mounting pressures on the domestic currency, the Bank of Guatemala (Banguat) started to intervene in the foreign exchange market to moderate the quetzal depreciation and tightened monetary policy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
